(VII)--one of कार्तवीर्यार्जुन's five sons who escaped;
1: Br. III. ४१. १३; M. ४३. ४६; वा. ९४. ७९; Vi. IV. ११. २१.
a महारथ;
2: Br. III. ६९. ५०.
in the course of a hunt he entered the hermitage of Jamadagni with sword in hand and killed him;
3: Ib. III. ४५. 1.
killed by परशुराम.
4: Ib. III. ४६. १७, २३.

--the people of शूरसेन territory. Fought with their kinsmen and ended their lives;
1: भा. I. १०. ३४; १५. ३९; IX. २४. ६३; XI. ३०. १८; वा. ४५. ११०.
a kingdom of मध्यदेश;
2: Br. II. १६. ४१; III. ७४; १३८.
the tribe with शूर as their chief: पञ्च- rathas: honoured Sagara and were killed by परशुराम;
3: Ib. III. ४५. 1; ४६. १७; ४९. 5; M. ११४. ३५.
kings of the line, १७ in number.
4: Ib. २७२. १७.
[page३-458+ ३२]

(IV)--the favourite wife of उत्तानपाद and mother of Uttama;
1: Vi. I. ११. 2
took Dhruva to task for getting into his father's lap and asked him to go to forest. It was predicted that she would die falling into forest fire; welcomed Dhruva returning from tapas;
2: भा. IV. 8. 8-२३, ४१-7.
insulted Dhruva, the son of the king by सुनीति.
3: Vi. I. ११. 7, १०.

(I)--is मार्ताण्ड as he occupies the inanimate globe; is हिरण्यगर्भ being born of the Golden Egg. By his course are divided all the worlds: the Lord of all, animate and inanimate: His movement among the राशीस् in the sky. Traversing the signs of मेष and तुला (the Goat and Balance) he makes days and nights of equal length: travers- ing the five signs commencing with वृषभ (Bull) he makes days longer and nights shorter in a month by २४ minutes: traversing the five signs commencing with वृश्चिक, he reverses the process. Rides in a chariot of one wheel with अरुण as charioteer. Sixtythousand वालखिल्यस् go in front of him singing the Vedas: is also served by other sages, Gan- dharvas, Apsaras, नागस्, यक्षस्, यातुधानस्, and Gods;
1: भा. V. २०. ४३-6; २१ (whole).
the sun moves with Meru and Dhruva on his right and marches towards the signs of the Zodiac. The twelve signs are the twelve months of a year. If he traverses one-sixth of the orbit, it is ऋतु, and if he completes one-half of his heavenly path it is ayana. Sometimes the velocity is slow, sometimes rapid and moderate: the name of the year differs accord- [page३-684+ ६०] ingly.
2: Ib. २२. 1-7.
also known as Divaspati and दिवाकर; १०० thousand yojanas from the earth, and the same distance from moon;
3: Br. IV. 2. २०, २९.
does not shine in इलावृतम्;
4: Ib. II. १७. १०.
protects the earth and hence Ravi;
5: Ib. II. २०. ५८; Ch. २१.
cosmology of; sunrise at Samyamana, midday at Ama- रावती; evening for विभा and midnight for सुखा. His rays enter fire during nights and come back during mornings; hence waters are warm during nights and cool during days; in a मुहूर्त सूर्य spreads over a lakh and ८१,000 yojanas;
6: Ib. II. Ch. २२-3; M. Ch. १२८.
chariot of one wheel with vedic metres as horses; colour of the sun in six seasons different; parent of the worlds, all birth and devastation due to him.
7: Br. II. Ch. २४.
Twelve-fold आत्म; instructed याज्ञवल्क्य in the form of a horse the यजुस्;
8: Ib. II. ३५. २३-5.
father of the Yuvati class of Apsaras; a friend of king सत्राजित्.
9: Ib. III. 7. २१, २१५; ७१. २१, २९.
Relative size of sun, moon, etc.; relative splendours, motions and qualities; different classes of rays named;
१०: M. Ch. १२८. १३-74.
survives antara pralaya; came after ब्रह्मा in the order of creation;
११: Ib. 2. १२ and ३१.
श्राद्ध deva;
१२: Ib. १३. 1.
Sunday sacred to:
१३: Ib. ७०. ३३.
fight with कालनेमि.
१४: Ib. १५०. १५१-179; २६८. ११.

(II)--a son of कश्यप and Aditi; wives सम्ज्ञा and छाया; father of Manu, श्राद्धदेव and Yama and Yami; see Vivasvan.
1: भा. VI. 6. ३९-41; IX. 1. १०-11.
Presented पृथु with arrows from h{??} rays; worship of: in प्लक्षद्वीप,
2: Ib. V. १५. १८; २०. 4-5.
begot a son on पृथा, still a maiden;
3: Ib. IX. २४. ३२. 5.
presented his friend सत्राजित with Syamantaka (s.v.);
4: Ib. X. ५६. 3.
propitiated by याज्ञवल्क्य, imparted to him वाजस- म्यष्ट यजुस् in the form of a horse.
5: Ib. XII. 6. ६६-74.
Pointed out with Soma, राहु in deva's disguise. Hence राहु chases him in parvas. Fought with बाण in देवासुर war;
6: Ib. VIII. 9; २४-6; १० 30.
बडवा was another wife, and Tapati daughter;
7: Ib. VIII. १३. 8-१०; IX. २२. 4.
is विभावसु ten Kalas of;
8: Br. I. २१. ८३.
gives life to Agni.
9: Ib. IV. ३५. ८१-3.
(आदित्य): came to कार्तवीर्य Arjuna in Brah- man's disguise and asked for a gift of all स्थावर for his food and offered in turn bows ever effulgent to help in burning [page३-685+ २७] down all स्थावरस्;
१०: M. 2. ३१; ४४. 3-११.
माहात्म्य of, in the भविष्य;
११: Ib. ५३. ३१.
the day sacred to the sun is the one when Hastam and Saptami fall on the same day;
१२: Ib. 5. 4.
is राहु's abode;
१३: Ib. १२७. १०.
knows what शिव did to पूष and Bhaga;
१४: Ib. १५५. 7.
through सरस्वती, got his two sons (not named);
१५: Ib. १७१. ५७-8.
worship of, by Brahmans.
१६: Ib. १८४. ३१.

--the Gandharva presiding over the month of ऊर्ज; a Mauneya Gandharva;
1: भा. XII. ११. ४४; Br. III. 7. 2; २३. २१; वा. ६९. 2.
with the sun in the months of माशि and Panguni;
2: Ib. ५२. २१.
in the sun's chariot during the फाल्- guna month.
3: Vi. II. १०. १८.
